  "user_request_original": "Design a 29-layer planar dielectric filter for 1550 nm LiDAR receiver. Incident medium: air. Substrate: fused silica. Materials: Ta2O5 (Gao) (high index) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) (low index), alternating sequence starting with Ta2O5 (Gao) at the air side. Layer sequence: Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao) (29 layers total, layer 15 is the central defect). Initialize all layer thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness at 1550 nm (Ta2O5 (Gao): approximately 1550/(4*n_Ta2O5 (Gao)), SiO2 (Lemarchand): approximately 1550/(4*n_SiO2 (Lemarchand))). Set thickness bounds to [30, 450] nm for layers 13-17 (cavity region), and [50, 400] nm for all other layers. Allow all 29 layer thicknesses to be optimized via gradient-based methods. Optimization objectives: maximize mean transmittance over 1545-1555 nm wavelength band, minimize mean transmittance over 1400-1500 nm band, minimize mean transmittance over 1600-1700 nm band. Use coherent transfer-matrix method at normal incidence. Simulation wavelength grid must span 1400-1700 nm with sufficient resolution to resolve the narrow passband.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize the thickness of a 29-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric filter on fused silica for a LiDAR receiver centered at 1550 nm. Maximize mean transmittance in 1545-1555 nm while minimizing mean transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm using coherent transfer-matrix calculations at normal incidence.",
